{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083451-of-the-dragon-s-son-dracula-or-his-final-fate-in-your-chronicle","id":1083451,"title":"Of the Dragon's Son - Dracula or his final fate in your chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-25T07:38:54-07:00","id":1083451,"title":"Of the Dragon's Son - Dracula or his final fate in your chronicle","content":"So, I'm feeling like writing. Have some fluff regarding what may have happened to Vlad Tepes Dracula in the world of Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A great many of us say we want to follow in Dracula's footsteps. Too many of us, perhaps. Some are looking towards him and where he might have gone as a great teacher, a source of unthinkable wisdom. This is itself, foolishness. To paraphrase the saying, &quot;If you meet Dracula on the road, stake him&quot;. We have no need for a great teacher, a head of a cult or some greater power to be leashed to like a dog. Structure is to teach. Structure is to show the foolish that they are foolish. It is to teach lessons that come from the outside, those that cannot find it themselves. But once set on the path to transcendence, it is foolish to look for anything other than your own personal strength. And yet, it is my begrudging duty to put to pen the most common and thoroughly researched theories we have available to us.<br /> <br /> First, that Dracula was never subject to revenant embrace at the hands of the Christian god. This is foolish and its research relies on human sources and human sources alone, citing the political, vicious, and perhaps even so far as to claim revisionist nature of Kindred society. Perhaps it is true, as many accounts exist of his mortal activities and the location of his body after death. However, false evidence of this magnitude is a routine occurrence. But then say they, all the more shocking that it would be true evidence, correct?<br /> <br /> Second, that Dracula still walks among us, playing whatever role he pleases for power unimaginable leads to unrestrained will. Truly, if this is correct then he does not desire the role of a grand tyrant lest he make his authority known. It is more likely that his agenda runs deeper and, perhaps, stranger than many of us are truly aware of. Likewise, if his conquest of the sun is to be believed then ultimately how shall we recognize a corpse-man who walks beneath the sun with nary a blister or scar? We would certainly not take him for kindred.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, that Dracula slumbers. The Blood's influence takes its toll on all of us, and we all find torpor to creep alongside us before a drastic overtaking like a maggot burrowing through whatever foul substance its will chooses. Perhaps the safest theory, yet one that ultimately bespeaks a manner of complacency. &quot;Why shall we have to care that Dracula exists, if we do indeed have greater certainty than not that he languishes in torpor still?&quot; to this I say, folly. We cannot ignore the concept that he may still walk among us, as one who has achieved transcendence must altogether be powerful and something that cannot be ignored.<br /> <br /> Finally and fourthly, that Dracula has transcended flesh, or the realms we see with all senses available to us. This reeks of a religion in the making, of dogma and doctrine that would only weigh us down. He was kindred. He is not now. If he has deposed the god of crusades and crosses on his throne, then he would have sent the angels in chains of darkness to witness this much to kindred and kine alike. Even perhaps thinking that he has become an archetype in the human mind more than a person is foolish, for it bespeaks perhaps thinking that he is no more than an idea now.<br /> <br /> But for all my report's approach, there is a truth that will remain. You will never in me find a god, a teacher, a servant, or a high master. You will never find me for who I am. I am not of your sort any longer. I am Transcendent.<br /> <br /> -Vladisaus, Son of the Dragon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","user":"BlitzKitty","date":". 04-25-2017, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:24:24-07:00","id":1083466,"title":"","content":"My personal world of darkness theory is simply that Vlad Dracul was only ever a human being. He was a cruel prince and he died and stayed dead, and then hundreds of years later a horror writer stole the name. That's all there ever was to Vlad Dracul.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul made him into a legend (what better way to give your occult society a pedigree then to have a famous monster-prince called back from the grave by the wrath of god give you his seal of approval) but it was only smoke and mirrors. There's a good reason he &quot;went into torpor and vanished&quot; once everything was codified. It's the order's deepest secret, and one they'd kill to protect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:51:02-07:00","id":1083479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083451-of-the-dragon-s-son-dracula-or-his-final-fate-in-your-chronicle?p=1083466#post1083466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal world of darkness theory is simply that Vlad Dracul was only ever a human being. He was a cruel prince and he died and stayed dead, and then hundreds of years later a horror writer stole the name. That's all there ever was to Vlad Dracul.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul made him into a legend (what better way to give your occult society a pedigree then to have a famous monster-prince called back from the grave by the wrath of god give you his seal of approval) but it was only smoke and mirrors. There's a good reason he &quot;went into torpor and vanished&quot; once everything was codified. It's the order's deepest secret, and one they'd kill to protect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I greatly prefer this kind of take, because among other things I'd like to think that the disciplines and their secrets go back much further with much more mysterious origins. That means there's something to investigate, and make enemies in doing so.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:12:05-07:00","id":1083486,"title":"","content":"&quot;You were a pawn, Vlad. The entirety of your undeath has been a tool to spread specific knowledge among your species. You are not the first to discover how the Curse might be weakened. You are merely the loudest. You are certainly not the first to rebel against divinity. Your rebellion just happened to be useful. Now, however, your part is done. You are more useful as a legend than a being. END.&quot;<br /> <br /> Realistically, Vlad's fate is something I would probably never answer. If I did though and I didn't need him alive for something...<br /> He gets to hear God's (or a decently ranked angel's) opinion of all his works and then he just disappears by divine command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:17:16-07:00","id":1083490,"title":"","content":"I know this thread is about fanon takes on Dracula, but I'd recommend checking out the text about his mortal life on pages 186-190 in Dark Eras. Many vampire players who aren't interested in DtD probably missed it since it's in a DtD centric Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:53:33-07:00","id":1084169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1083451-of-the-dragon-s-son-dracula-or-his-final-fate-in-your-chronicle?p=1083466#post1083466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal world of darkness theory is simply that Vlad Dracul was only ever a human being. He was a cruel prince and he died and stayed dead, and then hundreds of years later a horror writer stole the name. That's all there ever was to Vlad Dracul.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul made him into a legend (what better way to give your occult society a pedigree then to have a famous monster-prince called back from the grave by the wrath of god give you his seal of approval) but it was only smoke and mirrors. There's a good reason he &quot;went into torpor and vanished&quot; once everything was codified. It's the order's deepest secret, and one they'd kill to protect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really interesting approach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T16:56:56-07:00","id":1084209,"title":"","content":"In my CofD worlds, Drac's fate is always linked to whoever the &quot;real&quot; Van Helsing is, in some of my takes, Van Helsing defeated Dracula easily, in others it turns out like the Van Helsing movie, only for the hunter to realize he LIKES being a monster and in others, Dracula and the Van Helsing family are caught in a Batman-Joker situation where they NEED the battles between them to remain sane and give their existence meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}